  "verbalization": "Bupropion is associated with Anxiety Disorder through a chain of indications that link it to Major Depressive Disorder, which in turn is indicated to treat several neurotransmitter-related conditions. The evidence suggests that Bupropion may exert a role in the pathophysiology of Anxiety Disorder by influencing the treatment of Major Depressive Disorder, potentially through mechanisms involving neurotransmitter regulation or neurochemical pathways. The shared indication of Major Depressive Disorder across multiple paths implies a possible overlap in the therapeutic targets or biological mechanisms that underlie the relationship between Bupropion and Anxiety Disorder. The presence of multiple pathways pointing to Anxiety Disorder from different agents in the same clinical context supports the hypothesis that Bupropion may contribute to the treatment of anxiety through indirect mechanisms, possibly by modulating neurotransmitter systems that are also targeted in the treatment of depression.",
